Bump http-cache-semantics dependency floor to ^4.1.1 (GHSA-8x6c-cv3v-vp6g / CVE-2022-25881)

CVE-2022-25881 is a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) in the
transitive dependency http-cache-semantics, fixed in 4.1.1 (commit 560b2d8
"Don't use regex to trim whitespace" in kornelski/http-cache-semantics).
cacheable-request consumes http-cache-semantics for RFC 7234 cache handling;
the vulnerable parseCacheControl regex lives entirely in that dependency.

cacheable-request@6.1.0 declares "http-cache-semantics": "^4.0.0", which still
allows resolving to vulnerable 4.0.x–4.1.0 releases. Later cacheable-request
releases (7.0.3+, 11.0.0+) use ^4.1.1 as the dependency floor. This patch
aligns 6.1.0 with that remediated range.

GHSA-8x6c-cv3v-vp6g was withdrawn for cacheable-request because the issue is in
http-cache-semantics, but raising the floor prevents lockfiles from pinning a
pre-4.1.1 release and clears scanner false positives on this package version.

--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 	"dependencies": {
 		"clone-response": "^1.0.2",
 		"get-stream": "^5.1.0",
-		"http-cache-semantics": "^4.0.0",
+		"http-cache-semantics": "^4.1.1",
 		"keyv": "^3.0.0",
 		"lowercase-keys": "^2.0.0",
 		"normalize-url": "^4.1.0",
